<!--
  Fork build: no iCloud.

  Upstream signs with its own Team and claims `iCloud.com.robinebers.openusage`. A fork can't: Apple
  only issues a provisioning profile for a container owned by the signing Team, so keeping the
  entitlement here would fail signing for anyone but upstream. iCloud Sync is simply unavailable in
  fork builds; everything else — the local scanners, every provider card — is unaffected.

  To restore it, create a container under your own Team, put its id here and in release.sh's
  NSUbiquitousContainers, and pass ICLOUD_PROVISIONING_PROFILE.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict/>
</plist>
